-त्वयि त्रिलोकीभृति राज्यभारं निधाय नाभिः सह मेरुदेव्या ।तपोवनं प्राप्य भवन्निषेवी गतः किलानन्दपदं पदं ते ॥ 20.4 ॥
+त्वयि त्रिलोकीभृति राज्यभारं निधाय नाभिः सह मेरुदेव्या ।तपोवनं प्राप्य भवन्निषेवी गतः किलानन्दपदं पदं ते ॥20.4॥
-Simple Meaning: Having entrusted the burden of ruling the kingdom to You, the protector of the three worlds, King Nabhi retired to the forest of penance along with Merudevi. Devoting himself entirely to Your worship, he indeed attained Your supreme realm of eternal bliss.
-इन्द्रस्त्वदुत्कर्षकृतादमर्षात् ववर्ष नास्मिन्नजनाभवर्षे ।यदा तदा त्वं निजयोगशक्त्या स्ववर्षमेनद्व्यदधाः सुवर्षम् ॥ 20.5 ॥
-Word-by-word meaning: इन्द्रः Indra, त्वत्-उत्कर्ष-कृतात caused by Your excellence/greatness, अमर्षात् out of jealousy, ववर्ष न did not rain, अस्मिन् in this, अजनाभ-वर्षे realm of Ajanabha, यदा when, तदा then, त्वम् You, निज-योग-शक्त्या through Your own power of yoga, स्व-वर्षम् Your own realm, एनत् this, व्यदधाः made, सु-वर्षम् a land of abundant rain
+Simple Meaning: Having entrusted the burden of ruling the kingdom to You (in the incarnation of Rishabha), the protector of the three worlds, King Nabhi retired to the forest of penance along with Merudevi. Devoting himself entirely to Your worship, he indeed attained Your supreme realm of eternal bliss.
