-शयुव्रतं गोमृगकाकचर्यां चिरं चरन्नाप्य परं स्वरूपं ।दवाहृताङ्गः कुटकाचले त्वं तापान् ममापाकुरु वातनाथ ॥ 20.10 ॥
-Word-by-word meaning: शयु-व्रतम् the life of a python (staying still and accepting whatever comes), गो-मृग-काक-चर्याम् the lifestyle of a cow, a deer, and a crow, चिरम् for a long time, चरन् practicing, आप्य having attained, परम् supreme, स्व-रूपम् real nature/form, दव-आहृत-अङ्गः having Your body consumed by a forest fire, कुटक-अचले on Kutaka mountain, त्वम् You, तापान् afflictions/sufferings, मम my, अपाकुरु remove, वातनाथ O Lord of Guruvayur
-Simple Meaning: Observing the ways of the life of a python, and living like a cow, a deer, or a crow for a long time, You abided in Your supreme divine nature. Eventually, on Kutaka mountain, You allowed Your physical body to be consumed by a forest fire. O Lord of Guruvayur, please remove all my afflictions and sufferings!
